# ============================================================
# PQC-QKD Hybrid PoC — Sample environment file
# Copy to `.env` and adjust as needed. Never commit `.env`.
# ============================================================

# ----- Docker Compose -----
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=pqcqkd

# ----- Arnika (per-node; alice/bob entrypoints read these) -----
# Operational mode. See submodules/arnika/config/config.go:280 at the pin.
# Values: QkdAndPqcRequired | AtLeastQkdRequired | AtLeastPqcRequired | EitherQkdOrPqcRequired
# Every node reads this one variable, so both peers of a pair always agree,
# which arnika requires.
#
# The PQC half of the wg0 PSK is arnika's own PQC-HPKE key agreement with its
# peer (HPKE Base mode, RFC 9180, KEM MLKEM1024-P384 from draft-ietf-hpke-pq).
# Its switch, PQC_ENABLED, is not offered here: every compose file sets it to
# the literal "true" on every node, and QkdAndPqcRequired needs it.
ARNIKA_MODE=QkdAndPqcRequired

# Key rotation interval. arnika's own default is 10s, and its README recommends
# aligning with WireGuard's 120s rekey; 30s here so rotations show up quickly.
ARNIKA_INTERVAL=30s

# Shared secret between the two arnika peers. REQUIRED -- there is no default.
# It keys the AES-256-GCM encryption and HMAC-SHA256 signature applied to every
# arnika packet, key_ID and PQC-HPKE frames alike
# (submodules/arnika/auth/auth.go), and the per-interval master election
# (config/config.go, IsPrimary). Must be IDENTICAL on both, and at least 32
# bytes. The node entrypoints refuse the placeholder below, which is long
# enough to pass arnika's own length check.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
ARNIKA_PSK=replace-me-run-openssl-rand-base64-32

# Per-node numeric identifier, at most 5 digits. The two values MUST DIFFER IN
# PARITY (one odd, one even): arnika XORs this into the master election and
# reads only bit 0, so two IDs of the same parity -- equal or not -- make both
# peers pick the same role every interval and the key exchange deadlocks. Left unset,
# arnika derives it from the LISTEN_ADDRESS port -- which is :9999 on both
# nodes here, hence the explicit values.
ARNIKA_ID_ALICE=1
ARNIKA_ID_BOB=2
# Trusted-node relay, only used by the `multihop` profile. It peers with
# alice's second arnika instance, which reuses ARNIKA_ID_ALICE, so it must have
# the OPPOSITE PARITY to alice (only bit 0 is used). 3 was different but odd.
ARNIKA_ID_CHARLIE=4

# KMS HTTP timeout / retry
KMS_HTTP_TIMEOUT=10s
KMS_BACKOFF_MAX_RETRIES=5
KMS_BACKOFF_BASE_DELAY=200ms
KMS_RETRY_INTERVAL=10s

# ----- BB84-KME -----
# The physics tunables are not environment variables: the batch size, the
# channel and detector model, the QBER abort threshold, pool sizes and the Eve
# defaults all live in config/qkd_params.yaml.

# ----- WebUI -----
WEBUI_BACKEND_PORT=8000
WEBUI_FRONTEND_PORT=5173

# Let /physics change the LIVE KMEs (POST /api/sim/params, /api/sim/params/reset
# and /api/sim/backend). Those settings are process-global on both KMEs and
# feed arnika's key supply, so on any host more than one person can reach this
# must stay false: the routes then answer 403 and /physics edits only its
# in-browser model. true | false (1/true/yes/on enable it, anything else leaves
# it off). The backend's other switches -- ENABLE_CONTAINER_CONTROL, DEMO_MODE,
# the rate limit and the export bounds -- are NOT read from this file; see
# docs/BUILD.md section 7.1.
ENABLE_LIVE_PARAM_OVERRIDES=false

# ----- WireGuard internal addressing -----
# There is no subnet variable: the subnet is implied by these addresses and by
# each compose file's own network block. Each node's entrypoint puts the
# address on its interface with a /24.
#
# wg0, the hop tunnel keyed by arnika.
WG_ALICE_IP=10.0.0.1
WG_BOB_IP=10.0.0.2
WG_CHARLIE_IP=10.0.0.3
WG_LISTEN_PORT_ALICE=51820
WG_LISTEN_PORT_BOB=51821
WG_LISTEN_PORT_CHARLIE=51822
# wg1, the end-to-end data tunnel keyed by Rosenpass. Its peers are reached at
# their wg0 address on these ports, so wg1 runs inside wg0; it needs a subnet
# of its own, distinct from wg0's. The CHARLIE values are used only by the
# `multihop` profile.
WG1_ALICE_IP=10.0.1.1
WG1_BOB_IP=10.0.1.2
WG1_CHARLIE_IP=10.0.1.3
WG1_LISTEN_PORT_ALICE=51830
WG1_LISTEN_PORT_BOB=51831
WG1_LISTEN_PORT_CHARLIE=51832

# ----- ETSI 014 transport -----
# No TLS switch: the arnika-to-KME link is plain HTTP on the internal network
# (docs/LIMITATIONS.md).
